#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""check-blast — detect high-blast-radius changes, so they can be gated rather than merged quietly.

Phase 4 step 6 (combination plan §5A "The automation principle", the "Never automated" band and
its "Enforce it, don't just declare it" bullet): resolving a contradiction, deleting knowledge, and
promoting repo -> general are never automated. This is the CI gate that enforces that bullet: "A CI
gate blocks auto-merge of any PR that deletes a knowledge/ file, resolves a contradictions.md entry,
or moves a file repo->general, unless a label writable only by a domain owner (not the agent
identity) is set."

THE OWNER'S DECISION FOR THIS STEP (recorded in documents/state-change-gates.md): a CI gate, admin
bypass kept. The plan's paired bullet — 2 reviewers + a 24h window for high-blast-radius facts — is
left DORMANT until a second owner exists: ADR-0002 already establishes that a single contributor
cannot constitute two approvals or a second reviewer, and the same reasoning applies unchanged to
two reviewers on a high-blast PR. Nothing here builds that half.

DETECTION ONLY. This script changes nothing — it reads a diff and reports every high-blast finding
on stdout. Gating on a positive finding (failing a required status check, requiring a label to pass)
is CI's job, wired into .github/workflows/guardrails.yml and documents/library-guardrails.yml, never
this script's.

TWO REPO KINDS, told apart by what sits at the repo root — the same distinction CONVENTIONS §1/§2
draws in prose: CONVENTIONS.md exists ONLY in the engine (ADR-0007 — "the engine holds no domains";
a library holds content, not the contract), and a root INDEX.md exists ONLY in a library ("INDEX.md
at the library root is the domain router"; the engine has no domain to route, so it has none). A
repo with neither is not one check-blast recognizes — usage error, not a silent guess at which
rules apply.

WHAT COUNTS AS A "FACT FILE" (library repos): any tracked *.md file, outside documents/, plugins/,
scripts/, .github/, .githooks/, .claude-plugin/, .claude/ and .git/ (the same NON_KB exclusion
check-kb and check-scope already use), EXCEPT an INDEX.md at any level (a router, not a fact) and a
*-golden.md (the test oracle, not a fact — its own removal is already check-golden's job: "a library
with content and no oracle is untested by construction"). documents/ holds archived EVIDENCE
(CONVENTIONS §6), not the facts themselves, which is why it is excluded here rather than overlooked.

CONFLICTED-MARKER REMOVAL: counts occurrences of the inline `status: CONFLICTED` marker (CONVENTIONS
§8) in a file's old and new content — matched by path, or by old-path -> new-path across a detected
rename. A drop in count is a contradiction being resolved outside the review §8 requires ("do not
silently pick a winner"). Checked over every tracked knowledge file, not only "fact files" as
defined above, because a state leaf (a `<domain>-contradictions.md` register) can carry the same
inline marker syntax.

SCOPE PROMOTION: ADR-0004 draws one tier boundary explicitly — repo:<project> is a different HOME
(the project repository) from product:<vendor> / org:<company> / general, which all share ONE home
(the general root) and differ only in how wide a claim they make. Within that shared home, the
combination plan's own three-tier language (§2: "product/org-general, cross-repo" named as a single
middle tier, sitting between repo-specific and personal) ranks product: and org: together — both
narrower than an unqualified `general` claim, which asserts a truth with no vendor or company
qualifier at all. That gives the strict order used here:

    repo:<project>   <   { product:<vendor>, org:<company> }   <   general

A change from a narrower rank to a strictly higher rank is a promotion and is flagged.
product:<vendor> <-> org:<company> is a lateral reclassification (same rank, not a promotion toward
general) and is deliberately NOT flagged — §5A's named hazard is a fact moving toward the general
tier, not a fact being reclassified within it.

ENGINE-SIDE: any change — add, edit, delete or rename — that touches CONVENTIONS.md (the contract)
or a file under documents/decisions/ (the record). CODEOWNERS already marks both `@dhtaylor` at the
highest review bar; this is CI saying the same thing where a human reviewer might not be looking.

THE LABEL: `owner-approved`. Chosen over something like "high-blast-approved" because it names WHO
is attesting, not what is being approved — matching §5A's own phrasing, "a label writable only by a
domain owner." It reads the same on a library PR or an engine PR. NOTE (see
documents/state-change-gates.md): today, with one collaborator on each repository, this label is
writable by anyone with triage access — "writable only by a domain owner" is a property of there
being exactly one collaborator, not of any permission this script or the workflow enforces.

Usage: check-blast <base> <head> [--labels <comma,list>]
  Run inside a git repository (library or engine) that already has both <base> and <head> as
  resolvable commits (a shallow clone with the wrong depth will fail the diff, not silently pass).
  --labels   the PR's labels (e.g. names from github.event.pull_request.labels[].name), comma-
             separated. If 'owner-approved' is among them, findings still print, but the exit code
             is 0 rather than 1 — detection is not suppressed, only the gate is.
Exit 0 if no high-blast finding (or the owner label is present); 1 if any finding and no owner
label; 2 on a usage error (bad arguments, not a git repository, base/head do not resolve, or the
repo root has neither CONVENTIONS.md nor INDEX.md).
"""
import pathlib, re, subprocess, sys

NON_KB = {"documents", "plugins", "scripts", ".github", ".githooks",
          ".claude-plugin", ".claude", ".git"}
OWNER_LABEL = "owner-approved"
CONFLICTED_RE = re.compile(r"^\s*status:\s*CONFLICTED\b", re.M)
SCOPE_RE = re.compile(r"^scope:\s*(\S+)\s*$", re.M)
# ADR-0004 / plan §2: repo: is a different HOME; product:/org: share the general
# root and are ranked together, narrower than an unqualified general claim.
RANK = {"repo": 0, "product": 1, "org": 1, "general": 2}


def run(*args):
    return subprocess.run(args, capture_output=True, text=True)


def repo_root():
    p = run("git", "rev-parse", "--show-toplevel")
    return pathlib.Path(p.stdout.strip()) if p.returncode == 0 else None


def repo_kind(root: pathlib.Path):
    if (root / "CONVENTIONS.md").is_file():
        return "engine"
    if (root / "INDEX.md").is_file():
        return "library"
    return None


def in_kb(path: str) -> bool:
    parts = pathlib.Path(path).parts
    return path.endswith(".md") and not (NON_KB & set(parts))


def is_fact_file(path: str) -> bool:
    if not in_kb(path):
        return False
    name = pathlib.Path(path).name
    return name != "INDEX.md" and not name.endswith("-golden.md")


def tier_rank(scope: str):
    return RANK.get(scope.split(":", 1)[0])


def show(ref: str, path: str):
    """Content of path at ref, or None if it does not exist there."""
    p = run("git", "show", f"{ref}:{path}")
    return p.stdout if p.returncode == 0 else None


def diff_entries(base: str, head: str):
    """[(status, old_path_or_None, new_path_or_None)], with rename detection (-M)."""
    p = run("git", "diff", "--name-status", "-M", base, head)
    if p.returncode != 0:
        return None, p.stderr
    out = []
    for line in p.stdout.splitlines():
        if not line.strip():
            continue
        fields = line.split("\t")
        status = fields[0]
        if status.startswith("R"):
            old_path, new_path = fields[1], fields[2]
        elif status == "A":
            old_path, new_path = None, fields[1]
        elif status == "D":
            old_path, new_path = fields[1], None
        else:  # M, T, C ...
            old_path, new_path = fields[1], fields[1]
        out.append((status, old_path, new_path))
    return out, None


def find_blast(base: str, head: str, kind: str):
    entries, err = diff_entries(base, head)
    if err is not None:
        return None, err
    findings = []

    if kind == "library":
        for status, old_path, new_path in entries:
            if old_path and is_fact_file(old_path) and new_path != old_path:
                if new_path is None:
                    findings.append((old_path, "fact file deleted"))
                else:
                    findings.append((old_path, f"fact file renamed to {new_path} — the slug "
                                                f"changes; a citation naming the old slug goes dead"))

            if not (old_path and new_path and in_kb(old_path) and in_kb(new_path)):
                continue
            old_text, new_text = show(base, old_path), show(head, new_path)
            if old_text is None or new_text is None:
                continue

            old_n, new_n = len(CONFLICTED_RE.findall(old_text)), len(CONFLICTED_RE.findall(new_text))
            if new_n < old_n:
                findings.append((new_path, f"removes a CONFLICTED marker ({old_n} -> {new_n}) — "
                                            f"resolving a contradiction is never automated (CONVENTIONS §8)"))

            old_m, new_m = SCOPE_RE.search(old_text), SCOPE_RE.search(new_text)
            if old_m and new_m and old_m.group(1) != new_m.group(1):
                old_scope, new_scope = old_m.group(1), new_m.group(1)
                old_rank, new_rank = tier_rank(old_scope), tier_rank(new_scope)
                if old_rank is not None and new_rank is not None and new_rank > old_rank:
                    findings.append((new_path, f"scope promoted {old_scope} -> {new_scope} — "
                                                f"toward the general tier (ADR-0004)"))

    elif kind == "engine":
        for status, old_path, new_path in entries:
            touched = {p for p in (old_path, new_path) if p}
            label = new_path or old_path
            if "CONVENTIONS.md" in touched:
                findings.append((label, "CONVENTIONS.md changed — the contract every library conforms to"))
            if any(p.startswith("documents/decisions/") and p.endswith(".md") for p in touched):
                findings.append((label, "decision record changed — the record of why, not just what"))

    return findings, None


def main(argv):
    labels, pos = set(), []
    i = 0
    while i < len(argv):
        a = argv[i]
        if a == "--labels":
            if i + 1 >= len(argv):
                print("usage: check-blast <base> <head> [--labels <comma,list>]", file=sys.stderr)
                return 2
            labels = {s.strip() for s in argv[i + 1].split(",") if s.strip()}
            i += 2
        elif a.startswith("--labels="):
            labels = {s.strip() for s in a.split("=", 1)[1].split(",") if s.strip()}
            i += 1
        else:
            pos.append(a)
            i += 1
    if len(pos) != 2:
        print("usage: check-blast <base> <head> [--labels <comma,list>]", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    base, head = pos

    root = repo_root()
    if root is None:
        print("check-blast: not a git repository", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    kind = repo_kind(root)
    if kind is None:
        print(f"check-blast: {root} has neither CONVENTIONS.md nor INDEX.md at its root — "
              f"not a recognized repo kind", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2

    findings, err = find_blast(base, head, kind)
    if err is not None:
        print(f"check-blast: cannot diff {base}..{head}: {err.strip()}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2

    for path, reason in findings:
        print(f"BLAST {path}: {reason}")

    approved = OWNER_LABEL in labels
    if findings:
        note = f" — '{OWNER_LABEL}' label present, not blocking" if approved else ""
        print(f"\ncheck-blast: {len(findings)} high-blast finding(s) in {kind} repo{note}")
    else:
        print(f"\ncheck-blast: clean ({kind} repo, {base}..{head})")

    return 0 if (not findings or approved) else 1


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
